# sulabhkatiyar/gha-compute-smoke

Built on GitHub Actions by the public repository
[sulabh-research/gha-compute-smoke](https://github.com/sulabh-research/gha-compute-smoke), which holds all the code
that produces this dataset.

This dataset is the **canonical reference example** of a gha-compute workload: a deliberately tiny
smoke test (3000 rows of `openai/gsm8k`, a trivial deterministic text transform) that proves the build,
resume and publishing path end to end. The repository README and the operator guidelines
(`cloud_quota/github_actions.md` in the operator's utilities repository) describe how it works.

Each config of the repository (`configs/<config>.yaml`) is a separate subset in the viewer, stored under
`data/<config>/`. Every config has its own section below with its provenance and source licences.
Per-shard details (run attempt, source, parts) are in `_provenance/<config>/` and `_state/<config>/`.

## Licences

- This dataset: `mit`. Each source dataset and its licence is listed in its config's section.
- Code that built it: `MIT` (see the repository).

## Columns

`row_id` (global source row index), the source columns listed in the config's `keep_columns`,
`text_normalized` (NFKC, whitespace-collapsed, case-folded `text_column`), `n_chars`, `n_words`, `text_sha256`.

## Access

Access is gated (`auto`): requests are approved automatically.

